php/cakephp/milestones/7/labels","id":453043,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNDUzMDQz","number":7,"title":"3.0.0","description":"New major release that breaks compatibility with 2.x\r\n\r\n- PHP5.4.19+\r\n- New ORM & behaviors.\r\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":22,"created_at":"2014-07-07T19:51:41Z","updated_at":"2014-07-11T12:29:23Z","closed_at":"2014-07-11T12:29:23Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"trying to find some records with a statement similar to\n\n``` php\nTableRegistry::get('Merchants')->find()->contain(['MerchantTypes','BusinessProfiles'])\n```\n\nIn the developer enviroment I have 10 merchants, but the result return 0 results. \n\nRelations:\nMerchants -> belongsTo -> MerchantTypes\nMerchants -> hasOne -> businessProfiles\n\nI could see that the table business_profiles is empty and if the businessProfile record does not exist for each merchant then the result only return mechants with valid businessProfiles, however if the MerchantType does not exists or if null then the result return all the records with the MerchantType null. I think in the case of HasOne should be similiar to belongsTo and return a null in the related object. \n\nthis cause that will be impossible edit a record with hasOne and non existent relation, very common when the developer create a new relation, which is my case, I expect that the user create